# Presentation

Read `docs/system/presentation.md` before adding or changing a screen.

- Android and desktop share one MVI `ViewModel` in `:sharedUI`. It extends Lifecycle `ViewModel`, exposes one `StateFlow` of immutable state, and accepts events only through `onIntent`.
- One-off navigation and messages are an effect `Flow` from a `Channel`. The ViewModel does not take a `NavController` and does not import Compose.
- The composable collects state with `collectAsStateWithLifecycle` and sends intents. `remember` is only for focus and gesture state.
- iOS uses one `@Observable` screen model with `private(set)` state and a single `send` method. It calls `SharedLogic` domain types. Do not use `ObservableObject`, a Kotlin `ViewModel`, or an MVI framework.
- Do not put screen state in the `SharedLogic` framework.

```kotlin
fun onIntent(intent: AccountIntent) {
    when (intent) {
        AccountIntent.Opened -> refresh()
        is AccountIntent.AmountChanged -> _state.update { it.copy(amount = intent.value) }
    }
}
```
